<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

* ''MED — fallback kill can leave Codex descendants running'' ([[launch-codex.mjs|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.mjs:431]]): if the group signal fails, the fallback kills only the direct child PID. Codex-spawned processes can survive after the supervisor waits for the child and returns. The throwing-signal test checks only the shell PID ([[launch-codex.test.mjs|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.test.mjs:807]]), so it would miss surviving descendants.

* ''LOW — run.log assertion doesn’t verify held-directory behavior'' ([[launch-codex.test.mjs|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/launch-codex.test.mjs:642]]): `readFileSync(...) !== null` is true for any successfully read file, including an empty one. It doesn’t show that child output lands through the inherited directory handle.

The fd mapping itself looks correct: stdio array index 3 maps the held fd to supervisor fd 3; the Codex spawn maps only fds 0–2, so fd 3 is not passed through. I found no defect in the checked append, symlink-open, step-claim, temp-file, or placement-before-create paths.

<<~/ahu>>

